- * left its IOVA behind, and the UI allocates and frees tens of megabytes per
- * frame (measured: `gem_new 0x1400000 refused` after about twenty frames).
- * Every new IOVA also needs a new L2/L3 table, so the exhaustion showed up
- * twice. Keep the freed ranges and first-fit from them.
+ * The arena is one contiguous window (MONDRIAN_UC_IOVA_BASE.._END) and every
+ * GEM buffer takes a range in it. It started as a bump pointer, then kept 128
+ * freed ranges and first-fit from them, which is enough for a bring-up boot and
+ * not for a day of frames: the list gives up the range it cannot record, so the
+ * bump keeps moving and the tail of the window is eventually all a large
+ * allocation has left. Measured 2026-11-20 on a boot 3 h old: 9 479
+ * `MondrianGPU: gem_new 0x1400000 refused` (and 0xa00000, 0x700000, 0x500000,
